  "revision": "2026-09-05-fit-sign-correction",
  "model_formula": "packet_delta = -ROT(mirror, rotation) @ H_view",
  "source_sha256": {
    "Inputs/DualWeaponAuthored/accepted-act/female-assassin-pair28-attack-body-guide.act": "6126c72516f1cb165439c79e251ac265480ea0e82e832a42679f1b302e562d67",
    "Inputs/DualWeaponAuthored/sockets/female-assassin-attack.csv": "e4586e462678f9c0775966604496ea20cf4fffa59cdf8f989c01bf5b330d608a",
    "Inputs/DualWeaponAuthored/poses/female-assassin-pair28.csv": "7329786d42a9fbcaa9c0975251349702b434f6251c9023b655469c3b229cc898",
    "tools/dual_hilt_fit_validate.py": "79c68b0d007be5d2d88609bab2c54eeea6ff61768cdc2bfa87c860e5bff8c190"
  },
  "methodology": "Socket = accepted-act layer1 (pair_guide) x/y per (direction,frame), extracted by tools/dual_socket_extract.py (report 1 established this, not layer0/body_guide, is the anchor the weapon-layer deltas are authored against). Per-view hilt landmark H_view (one fixed (hx,hy) for view45/sword/hand0 and one for view34/dagger/hand1) was fit by least squares on 3 calibration cells per hand with distinct mirror+rotation combinations (direction,frame) = (0,0),(2,1),(4,2), using the ACT layer's own raw baked rotation and mirror flag. The fit targets negative CSV delta, matching T-socket=-R*H during validation. 8 distinct mirror-axis/order/rotation-sign conventions (16 equivalent parameter combinations) were brute-forced per hand (rotation direction and mirror application order are not pinned down by either research report); the convention minimizing calibration residual was kept. Predicted position = solve translation T = socket - R(mirror,rotation)*H_view, then re-expressed as a socket-relative delta T-socket for direct comparison against the CSV's packet_delta x/y (the socket value algebraically cancels out of this per-cell delta comparison; it is still explicit in the pipeline because it is what the model composes against, and matters for reconstructing an absolute screen position outside the scope of this check). Mirror check = ACT layer mirror bit vs CSV mirror column, direct equality. Angle check = ((act_rotation+180)%360)-180 vs CSV angle_deg (report 1 Q4 formula), tolerance 0.5deg.",
